  "consts": [
   "core/parsers/celio.py - CELIO France PO (Implant order \"IMP\").\n\nLayout (e.g. PO 60127501 POSTRAM, 6 pages):\n  page 0  - header block (PO number / Season / Shipping mode / Incoterm /\n            Payment terms / delivery date / MI) + the STANDARD packaging\n            line-item block (one row per colour x size, EU decimals).\n  page 1/3/5 - \"Terms of buying\" boilerplate (ignored).\n  page 2  - the Homogene packaging line-item block + a size-breakdown matrix\n            (``XXXS XXS XS S M L XL XXL XXXL`` header, then one row per colour\n            with ``/`` empty markers + per-size qty + a trailing total) + the\n            final ``BOX ORDERED / PIECES ORDERED / TOTAL AMOUNT`` summary.\n  page 4  - signature block (ignored).\n\nKey facts:\n  * Per-size quantities are taken from the size-breakdown matrix (already the\n    combined STANDARD+Homogene totals), NOT from re-summing the two line-item\n    blocks whose rows wrap awkwardly across lines.\n  * European numbers: dot = thousands separator, comma = decimal (``1.110``,\n    ``9,50``, ``45.495,50``).\n  * Prices: the column aligned under ``UNIT PRICE`` is the USD cost/FOB price\n    (``9,50 USD``); the ``39,99 EUR`` value sits in an unlabelled retail-price\n    column and is NOT the PO amount. The PO totals are USD, so the OSR\n    ``Unit Price`` = USD price and ``Currency`` = USD.\n\nISOLATED: self-contained; does not touch matrix_* / line_items / control_sheet /\ncostco_* / line_items_eu.\n",
